y Commissioners\nEconomic Vitality Incentive Program\nEmployment\nForms & Worksheets\nRequest for Bids/Proposals\nZoning\nTownships\nBurdell Township\nCedar Township\nEvart Township\nHartwick Township\nHersey Township\nHighland Township\nLeRoy Township\nLincoln Township\nMarion Township\nMiddle Branch Township\nOrient Township\nOsceola Township\nRichmond Township\nRose Lake Township\nSherman Township\nSylvan Township\nVisitors\nChambers of Commerce\nCounty Profile\nCounty Parks\nPhoto Gallery\nShare this page\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://migration.revize.com/revize/HTML_Review/osceolami/freeform-fullwidth.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nPrev Next\nSub Menu\nRelated Pages & Links\nCounty Department Directory\nFees\nForms\nHelpful Links\nOnline Land Records Search\nRecording Requirements\nSearching\nTransfer Tax\nRegister of Deeds\nHeather E. Gray\n301 W. Upton Ave.\nReed City, MI 49677\nPhone (231) 832-6113\nFax (231) 832-6115\nregister@osceolacountymi.gov\nHome Government County Departments Register of Deeds\nRegister of Deeds\nREGISTER OF DEEDS\nHeather E. Gray, Register\n301 West Upton Avenue\nReed City, MI 49677\nPhone (231) 832-6113\nFax (231) 832-6115\nregister@osceolacountymi.gov\nONLINE LAND RECORDS SEARCH\nIf you need assistance with searching online, please read:\nHow to Search for Documents by a Name\nHow to Search for a Plat\nHow to Print Documents\n**NEW! Legal description searching is now available online!**\nRead How to Search by Legal Description for more information.\nFRAUD NOTIFY\nRegister your name and email address to be notified when a document has been recorded with your name.\nIf you need assistance with signing up, please read:\nHow to Sign Up for Fraud Notify Alerts\nGIS PARCEL MAPS\nUse this link to access Osceola County parcel maps.\nOUR STAFF\nHeather Gray - Register of Deeds\nJohnell Deline - Chief Deputy\nPatricia Todd - Deputy\nHOURS OF OPERATION\nMonday - Friday, 9:00 am to 5:00 pm, except holidays\nPublic terminal computers are available 9:00 am - 4:45 pm\nTHE REGISTER OF DEEDS\nServes as the official recording office for all documents pertaining to real estate.\nServes as the keeper of permanent land records, records dating back to 1853.\nMaintains full tract index by legal description of all parcels in the County.\nServes on Plat Board as chairperson.\nMISSION STATEMENT\nTo administer the Michigan statutes as they apply to the Register of Deed’s Office.\nTo provide service and information as to the public records regarding real property located in Osceola County.\nTo promptly process and accept for public record documentation complying with the Michigan Recording Act.\nTo research and develop new ways of using technology to improve the input, retrieval and storage of information.\nDisclaimer: Osceola County Register of Deeds does not endorse nor are we associated with any other web site which may attach itself by links to our website. This office does not prepare documents and does not answer legal questions. Please contact an attorney if you need legal assistance.\nAgendas / Minutes\n2026 Approved Budget for Osceola County\nEmployment\nFOIA Process\nForms & Worksheets\nRequest for Bids / Proposals\nVolunteer Opportunities\nCounty Departments\nYour Opinion Matters\nOsceola County Survey\nVolunteer for a Board or Commission\nOsceola County is an Equal Opportunity Employer\nUSDA Nondiscrimination Statement\nEmployee Resources\nDiscover Osceola County\nsearch\nOsceola County Main Courthouse\n301 W. Upton Avenue\nReed City, MI 49677\nPhone: Refer to Department Directory\n© 2020 Osceola County, MI. All rights reserved.\nPowered by , The Government Website Experts | Login\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nundefined\nundefined\nundefined",
